.TH USB-IF 1 "September 2026" "cv-suite-automator 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usb-if \- automate USB-IF CV Suite test runs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-if
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.PP
.B usb-if
.I CHIPSET
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usb-if
runs the interactive CV Suite automation workflow on a Windows 11 validation
host. It drives USB-IF CV Suite, controls the USB switchboard, and collects the
reports produced by the selected tests.
.PP
At startup, the program prompts for tests, host controllers, and USB protocol
modes. Press Enter at a selection prompt to select every available choice.
When both host controllers are selected, the operator is prompted once to move
the device between controller ports.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I CHIPSET
The bridge controller chipset name used to identify the test session, for
example
.BR 3861EN-FL .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a concise command-line usage summary and exit without initializing lab
hardware.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The command requires a Windows 11 validation host, USB-IF CV Suite, an unlocked
supported device, the Phidgets relay controller and USB2/USB3 switchboard, and
the configured external results drive.
.SH OUTPUT
Each run saves the CV Suite HTML reports and a
.B summary.json
file in a timestamped session directory on the configured results drive.
Reports are grouped by host controller and USB protocol.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The selected run completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The command was invoked incorrectly or the automation could not continue.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
usb-if "3861EN-FL"
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
The workflow is Windows-only and depends on lab-specific hardware and CV Suite
window behavior. A physical cable move is required when both host controllers
are selected.
